Hooks allow you to execute shell commands at various points in the apply/commit lifecycle.

**Example:**
```toml
[hooks]
pre_apply = [
    { command = "echo 'Starting apply...'" },
    { command = "systemctl --user restart some-service", conditions = { os = ["linux"] } }
]
post_apply = [
    { command = "notify-send 'Dotfiles applied'" }
]
pre_commit = [
    { command = "git add -A" }
]
post_commit = [
    { command = "git push", timeout = 60 }
]
```
